  "body": "**Issue**\r\nThe spec expects [m.call.candidates](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.9/client-server-api/#mcallcandidates) events to contain an array of `Candidates`, where each one has 3 **required** fields: `candidate`, `sdpMLineIndex` and `sdpMid`\r\n\r\n[The spec also says](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.9/client-server-api/#end-of-candidates) that end of discovery should be marked by `An ICE candidate whose value is the empty string`, which contradicts the Candidate definition.\r\n\r\nThis in turn causes problems on implementations that are strict about required fields e.g. [Ruma](https://github.com/ruma/ruma/blob/f24cae17f50d140a0ff112cb3dc74a2053aa1df4/crates/ruma-events/src/call/candidates.rs#L10-L37) which throws deserialization errors in this case.\r\n\r\n**Expected behaviour**\r\nThe spec should be clear about what Candidates can look like. Ideally they would've been typed but I guess that ship has sailed.",
